  body: "# Benefit weeks and changes of circumstances\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured payment
    chapter describes JSA and IS as weekly benefits, defines a benefit week as seven days with benefit-specific
    determination and separately routes changes of circumstances to supersession guidance.\n\n## Scope
    and exceptions\n\nA benefit week is not assumed to be a calendar week or identical across JSA and
    IS. The selected passages do not compute payment days, award amounts or effective dates; benefit-week
    changes, first or last weeks and other payment rules remain dependencies.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 33009, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n- [DMG 33010, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n- [DMG 33050, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch33`: PDF SHA-256 `8dfef5032a37a357a10503574a00872e4af713b89d2c83463e8ee948b33c38c1`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f62f3e307149fe6c547a171b9c4be4ec49d0b49855ba6ab87630c29ba132f3b7`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsais-part-week
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter separately addresses entitlement for part of a week instead of assuming
      every award covers a full benefit week.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch33/0005
      quote: "33009 JSA and IS are weekly benefits that are normally paid for complete weeks (benefit
        weeks). See\nDMG 33100 - 33238 for guidance on when payment may be made for part-weeks.\n\n\n\n\
        \nMeaning of benefit week"
      locator: DMG 33009
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch33/0013
      quote: "33100 This section gives guidance on how to calculate part-week payments in JSA and IS claims.\n\
        \n\n\n\nDefinitions\n\nMeaning of notional entitlement"
      locator: DMG 33100
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The change-of-circumstances passage identifies supersession as a possible decision
      ground and routes it to chapter 4.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch33/0010
      quote: "33050 A change in the claimant's circumstances can give grounds to supersede the award 1
        in both JSA\nand IS. The normal rules on supersession are in DMG Chapter 04.\n\n\n           \
        \                                                                          1 SS Act 98, s 10\n\
        \n\n33051 - 33059"
      locator: DMG 33050
